# Trust anchor for the managed Postgres TLS certificate.
#
# The database presents:
#   leaf  *.<cluster>.pg.ubicloud.app
#   inter ZeroSSL ECC DV SSL CA 2
#   cross Sectigo Public Server Authentication Root E46
#   root  USERTrust ECC Certification Authority   <- this file
#
# It is a public root, not a secret. It is committed because the pg gem
# ships its own libpq/OpenSSL, whose built-in OPENSSLDIR need not match the
# container's /etc/ssl/certs, so sslrootcert=system resolves to nothing and
# verification fails with "certificate verify failed" -- while psql, using
# the system libpq, succeeds against the very same URL.
#
# Verified: this root alone gives "Verify return code: 0 (ok)" with the
# system store disabled. Override with RQ_DB_CA_CERT if the issuer changes.
-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----
